&lt;div class=&quot;col-lg-6 content&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Residency in Germany is required. This role is currently fully remote&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;#LI-Remote&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At JFrog, we’re reinventing DevOps to help the world’s greatest companies innovate -- and we want you along for the ride. This is a special place with a unique combination of brilliance, spirit and just all-around great people. Here, if you’re willing to do more, your career can take off. And since software plays a central role in everyone’s lives, you’ll be part of an important mission. Thousands of customers, including the majority of the Fortune 100, trust JFrog to manage, accelerate, and secure their software delivery from code to production -- a concept we call “liquid software.” Wouldn&#39;t it be amazing if you could join us in our journey?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Solutions Engineer to be on the front lines, working closely with our strategic customers and prospects, guiding them on how to build robust and secured business critical DevOps and software development processes in the age of agentic development. You will work with our Sales, Product &amp;amp; Engineering teams to help customers understand the value of JFrog solutions from a technical and business perspective. If you love working with brilliant people, being part of an energetic team and changing the world of software, you might be the perfect Frog to join our team!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As a Senior Solutions Engineer at JFrog you will...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage with customers to ensure their success in their DevOps and DevSecOps&amp;nbsp; journey leveraging the JFrog Platform&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support JFrog&#39;s Technical Selling motion and significantly contribute to the customer journey to build technical win and championship&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Showcase JFrog’s technology and success in events and conferences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence the features and roadmap of JFrog products based on customer needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay current with the latest technology trends related to the DevOps and DevSecOps landscape&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To be a Senior Solution Engineer at JFrog you need...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years experience in Technical Sales or Sales Engineering positions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in building relationships with customers’ champions and senior stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in Docker, Kubernetes, CI/CD, git integrations and&amp;nbsp; build tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with AppSec tools (part or all) such as: SCA / SAST / SBOM Management / Container Security&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build software pipelines with various DevOps tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with cloud infrastructures - AWS / Azure / GCP - Mandatory&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with agentic development workflows and understanding of related technical elements: LLMs, MCPs, skills and prompts - is an advantage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience in software development role - is an advantage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Native German speaker
&lt;div class=&quot;mt-3 w-full empty:hidden&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;text-center&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt; Find  Jobs in Germany  on Arbeitnow

Apex.AI is an international software company developing safety-certified, developer-friendly, and scalable software for mobility and autonomous systems. Our technology enables companies to build software-defined vehicles and intelligent machines faster, safer, and more efficiently.  &nbsp;  


  We are looking for a   hands-on  IT Administrator / (Senior) IT Administrator      to take ownership of the day-to-day operation and continuous improvement of our IT environment in Germany while supporting our international teams.  &nbsp;  


  This is a highly practical role for someone who enjoys solving technical problems, administering systems, supporting users, and continuously improving IT infrastructure. You will work across   Linux and macOS endpoints, identity and access management, cloud services, networks, security tooling, and on-premises infrastructure  .  &nbsp;  

  You will be a key point of contact for IT topics in our Munich office and work closely with Engineering, DevOps, HR, and other business functions.  &nbsp;  


  In addition to your core IT responsibilities, you will have the opportunity to   develop your knowledge of Information Security and compliance  , including ISO 27001 and TISAX. Previous compliance experience is welcome but   not required  —we are looking for someone who is interested in learning and growing in this area.  &nbsp;  


  As Apex.AI grows, this role offers the opportunity to take on broader ownership and help shape the future of our IT function.  &nbsp;  
 &nbsp; 
  This role is located in our Munich office. Authorization to work in Germany is required.  

   What You’ll Do   


   Hands-on IT Administration  &nbsp;   




  Own and manage the day-to-day operation of our cloud and on-premises IT environment.&nbsp;  &nbsp;  






  Administer and support   Linux and macOS endpoints   throughout their lifecycle.&nbsp;  &nbsp;  






  Manage MDM, IAM, user accounts, permissions, SSO, and MFA.&nbsp;  &nbsp;  






  Administer cloud-based email, collaboration, and file-storage services.&nbsp;  &nbsp;  






  Manage employee access across internal systems and business applications.&nbsp;  &nbsp;  






  Configure, maintain, and troubleshoot wired and wireless networks.&nbsp;  &nbsp;  






  Manage VPN solutions, network segmentation, policies, and access rules.&nbsp;  &nbsp;  






  Administer and maintain on-premises and cloud-based servers.&nbsp;  &nbsp;  








  Manage endpoint security solutions, including EDR/antivirus, patching, encryption, and security policies.&nbsp;  &nbsp;  






  Implement and maintain integrations between different IT systems.&nbsp;  &nbsp;  






  Automate repetitive IT administration tasks wherever possible.&nbsp;  &nbsp;  






  Monitor systems and proactively identify and resolve issues before they impact users.&nbsp;  &nbsp;  




   IT Support &amp; Service Delivery  &nbsp;   




  Be a primary point of contact for IT support for employees in our Munich office and provide remote support to colleagues in other locations.&nbsp;  &nbsp;  






  Troubleshoot hardware, software, endpoint, network, account, and access issues.&nbsp;  &nbsp;  






  Manage IT support requests and ensure issues are resolved efficiently.&nbsp;  &nbsp;  






  Set up laptops, accounts, permissions, and required applications for new employees.&nbsp;  &nbsp;  






  Execute IT onboarding and offboarding for employees and contractors.&nbsp;  &nbsp;  






  Manage IT hardware inventory and device lifecycle.&nbsp;  &nbsp;  






  Maintain clear and useful technical documentation.&nbsp;  &nbsp;  






  Help create a reliable and user-friendly IT environment where employees can work effectively with minimal friction.&nbsp;  &nbsp;  




   IT Security &amp; Compliance  &nbsp;   


  You will have the opportunity to learn how to&nbsp;manage ISMS based on ISO 27

